<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea 3-yr yields end down on lower rates hope.</title>
<headline>S.Korea 3-yr yields end down on lower rates hope.</headline>
<text>
<p>Yields on three-year corporates closed slightly lower on Monday as expectations of lower interest rates boosted institutional buying, brokers said.</p>
<p>Three-month CD yields and overnight call rates edged up because of rising demand in the short-term money market.</p>
<p>* 3-yr corporates end at 12.25 pct from 12.39 on Saturday</p>
<p>* 3-mth CDs close at 12.60 pct from 12.55</p>
<p>* Overnight call average 11.70 pct from 11.04</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
</text>
